# SAOMMO — Contributor Onboarding Manual

**Document:** Band 8 — Contributor Onboarding Manual
**Project:** SAOMMO
**Purpose:** Onboarding for human contributors and AI agents
**Version:** 1.0
**Date:** 2026-08-15

---

# 1. Purpose

SAOMMO is an open-source VR MMORPG project. It welcomes outside contributions.

This document explains how a contributor (human or AI) should approach the project.

The README invites two paths:

1. **Use one of the existing project KI prompts** as the basis for your work.
2. **Contact the project owner by email** describing what you can offer.

This manual makes both paths concrete.

---

# 2. Before You Start

Before writing any code, asset, or document, you must:

1. Read **Band 1 — Master Vision**.
2. Read **Band 2 — Technical Architecture**.
3. Read the bands relevant to your contribution:
   * Gameplay work → Band 3
   * World/Lore work → Band 4 + Band 7
   * Art work → Band 5
   * AI-assisted work → Band 6
4. Inspect the existing implementation under `SAOMMOnew/`.
5. Check recent Git history for context.

If you do not understand why something is the way it is, ask before changing it.

---

# 3. Path A — Use a Project KI Prompt

The project ships six prompt documents (and additional supporting ones):

| Band | Topic                          | Use it when                                        |
| ---- | ------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |
| 1    | Master Vision                  | You need overall project context                   |
| 2    | Technical Architecture         | You are writing or modifying engine code           |
| 3    | Gameplay Bible                 | You are designing or changing gameplay systems     |
| 4    | World Bible                    | You are designing locations, regions, or ecology   |
| 5    | Art & Asset Bible              | You are working on visuals, meshes, materials, VFX |
| 6    | AI Development Manual          | You are an AI agent working on this project        |
| 7    | Story & Lore Bible             | You are writing narrative, quests, NPCs, lore      |
| 8    | Contributor Onboarding         | You are new to the project (this document)         |

Pick the band closest to your task.
Do not invent a new approach when an existing one covers your needs.

---

# 4. Path B — Contact the Project Owner

Use Path B when:

* You want to contribute a skill the project does not yet have a prompt for.
* You want to propose a major architectural or narrative change.
* You want long-term collaboration, not a single contribution.

In your email, include:

* Who you are (real name or handle).
* What you can do (programming, art, audio, narrative, testing, infra, etc.).
* What you want to work on (a specific system, asset, or document).
* Why you are interested in SAOMMO.
* A short proposal of your first concrete contribution.

Do not start large work before contact is acknowledged.

---

# 5. Choosing the Right Engine Version

The project documentation was originally written for **UE 5.4.4**.

The current implementation (`SAOMMOnew/SAOMMOnew.uproject`) uses **UE 5.8**.

**Rule for contributors:**

* Match the version actually installed for the project.
* Do not silently change the engine version.
* If your work requires a version change, document it as a Decision Log entry (see Band 6 §15).

