# 8. Required Reading Order for New Contributors

1. README
2. Band 1 — Master Vision
3. Band 2 — Technical Architecture
4. Band 7 — Story & Lore Bible
5. The band relevant to your task
6. Recent Git history
7. The relevant source files under `SAOMMOnew/Source/`

Skipping this order is the most common cause of misaligned contributions.

---

# 9. Contribution Workflow

```text
Propose scope
     ↓
Read relevant documentation
     ↓
Inspect existing code
     ↓
Plan minimal change
     ↓
Implement
     ↓
Verify (compile / test)
     ↓
Update documentation if needed
     ↓
Submit change (commit / PR / patch)
```

Rules:

* Keep changes small and reviewable.
* One logical change per commit.
* Commit messages must describe what changed and why.
* Do not rewrite working systems because you would do them differently.

---

# 10. What You Must Not Do

* Do not delete or replace project directories.
* Do not reset Git history.
* Do not change the engine version without approval.
* Do not introduce plugins that are not justified (see Band 6 §22).
* Do not overwrite lore, faction history, or world rules silently.
* Do not generate large amounts of code without verifying each system.

---

# 11. What You Are Encouraged To Do

* Ask questions when something is unclear.
* Document decisions as ADRs (see Band 6 §15).
* Improve existing systems through small, well-scoped changes.
* Add tests when introducing new logic.
* Translate documentation between German and English when possible.
* Help close gaps between Band 2's target architecture and the live `SAOMMOnew` module.

---

# 12. Communication Channels

Until dedicated channels exist:

* **Issues / Discussions:** GitHub repository
* **Direct contact:** Email the project owner (see README)
* **In-document questions:** Open a PR that proposes the change and explains the rationale

There is currently no Discord, Slack, or Matrix channel.
Do not invent one without authorization.

---

# 13. AI Agents Working on This Project

If you are an AI agent:

* Follow **Band 6 — AI Development Manual**.
* Operate only within your assigned role (Technical, Gameplay, World, Art, QA, Master).
* Respect the File Access Matrix concept (Band 6 §9).
* Do not present assumptions as established project facts.
* Prefer **small, reviewable, scoped changes** over mass generation.

---

# 14. Onboarding Checklist

Before submitting your first contribution:

- [ ] I have read Band 1, Band 2, and the band relevant to my task.
- [ ] I have read Band 7 if my work touches narrative or world.
- [ ] I have inspected the relevant source files.
- [ ] I have matched the live engine version.
- [ ] I have defined the scope of my change.
- [ ] I have planned the smallest possible diff.
- [ ] I have a way to verify my change (compile, test, or visual check).
- [ ] I know which documentation (if any) needs updating.
- [ ] I have a clear, specific commit message.

---

# 15. Closing Note

SAOMMO is built by many small, careful contributions, not by one large push.

If moving, fighting, and interacting with the world feels good, SAOMMO has a foundation worth expanding.

Help build that foundation.
